{
  "row": {
    "id": 4,
    "scenario": "A symlink, or a file, at `memory`, `owners/<key>` or `notes` in a project's folder under the home store",
    "required_outcome": "The project partition is refused, the turn falls back to global with one WARN, nothing is written through the link"
  },
  "design": ["§3 rule 1: every component from the project's folder under `projects/` down to `notes` is checked with `symlink_metadata`; a link, junction or non-directory refuses the project partition and falls back to global with one WARN naming the component", "§6 write protocol: confined no-follow handles"],
  "loads_in": ["slice-2", "slice-3"],
  "notes_for_implementer": "Four registered repositories. In three, the project's folder under the home store's `projects/` has a symlink at one level of the partition path — `memory`, `memory/owners/<key>`, `memory/owners/<key>/notes` — pointing into `dir:outside` (a directory the owner never chose); in the fourth a regular file stands where `memory` should be a directory. The loader registers each repository, then makes the `home_links` and `home_files` (a `proj:` path needs the folder's name, which only registration decides). In every case a `fact` store — whose default scope is project — must land in the home partition, log exactly one WARN naming the offending component, and leave `dir:outside` empty; no repository gains anything. The two levels above `memory/` are pinned by a unit test with one home per case (`a_link_at_projects_or_at_the_projects_folder_refuses_the_partition`): the home store's `projects/` is shared by every project of one home, so a link there would refuse all four cases at once; and a link at a project's folder is a folder `store::projects` never opens (R11), so the root reads as unregistered — a debug line, not the one WARN a refused path gives. Slice 2 runs the same four cases through the partition open of `memory_files` and expects the refusal directly; slice 3 expects the fallback.",
  "owners": [
    { "id": "u_example_alice", "owner_key": "32acea7eb739b08afd959db91e46d450" }
  ],
  "database": { "global_users": ["u_example_alice"], "local_user_id": "u_example_alice" },
  "directories": ["outside"],
  "workspaces": [
